  "result": "The `toString` implementation is in place and builds, but two of the 16 runs still fail. The cause is in `support/date.rs`, which is outside my file scope. Its `year_string` helper pads negative years to six digits (`-000001`), but the spec's DateString uses a four-digit padded year (`-0001`). The fix is a one-line change to `year_string` in that file, so I did not work around it in my file.\n\nImplemented `Date.prototype.toString` in `prototype_to_string.rs` using `date::this_time_value` for RequireInternalSlot and `date::to_date_string` for ToDateString. The build is clean and clippy reports no warnings. `./t262 built-ins/Date/prototype/toString/` gives 14 pass, 2 fail (`negative-year.js`, sloppy and strict).\n\nBLOCKED: `crates/kahvi-builtins/src/support/date.rs` `year_string` must pad negative years to 4 digits (`{:04}`), not 6 (`{:06}`), per DateString's ToZeroPaddedDecimalString(abs(yv), 4)",
